<%# "Tips & Tricks" — what the paperboy in the bottom-left corner opens.

    It lives in the layout because the mascot does, and it is opened by the
    `tips:open` window event so nothing has to reach it (see
    shared/_search_commands for the same pattern).

    Every tip here describes something the app actually does. The quick-search
    row is behind the same ACL check that decides whether ":" installs a
    keyboard listener at all — offering the shortcut to someone who does not
    hold the grant would just be a key that does nothing. %>
<div data-controller="tips"
     data-action="tips:open@window->tips#open">
  <div class="pb-modal-backdrop" hidden
       data-tips-target="modal"
       data-action="click->tips#backdropClose">
    <div class="pb-modal pb-modal--lg" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
         aria-labelledby="pb-tips-title">
      <div class="pb-modal__header">
        <h3 id="pb-tips-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h3>
        <button type="button" class="pb-modal__close" aria-label="Close"
                data-action="tips#close">&#10005;</button>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-modal__body">
        <ul class="pb-tips">
          <% if can_use_command_palette? %>
            <li class="pb-tip">
              <kbd class="pb-tip__key">:</kbd>
              <p class="pb-tip__text">
                <strong>Quick search.</strong> Press <kbd>:</kbd> anywhere you are
                not typing in a box to open the command palette — every form and
                command in the system, searchable from any app.
              </p>
            </li>
          <% end %>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <kbd class="pb-tip__key">Esc</kbd>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Close anything.</strong> Escape dismisses this dialog, the
              command palette, and every other dialog in the app.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <kbd class="pb-tip__key">&crarr;</kbd>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Enter runs the command.</strong> In the sidebar's search
              box, Enter fires whichever command is on offer instead of just
              filtering the list.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Ask "who am i".</strong> Type it into the sidebar search or
              the command palette to see your account and where you sit in the
              organization.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Search forms by more than name.</strong> The sidebar box
              matches numbers, fields and tags too — and
              <em>Advanced Search</em> underneath it narrows by the metadata an
              admin set in the form builder. The two compose.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Switch apps.</strong> The chevron beside the app name at
              the top of the sidebar moves between Paperboy, Data Runner and
              Chart of Accounts.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>My Work is three tabs.</strong> Inbox, Submissions and
              Records are one page — the badge counts what is waiting on you.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Choose your columns.</strong> The <kbd>+</kbd> above the
              table on Inbox, Submissions and Records opens
              <em>Customize columns &amp; filters</em>.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li class="pb-tip">
            <span class="pb-tip__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#9670;</span>
            <p class="pb-tip__text">
              <strong>Save a search.</strong> On Submissions,
              <em>Save Search</em> keeps a set of filters and puts it in the
              dropdown for next time.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-modal__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="tips#close">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
